WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.481
Comparing the robustness of the best possible
classifier to what state-of-the-art training

00:00:05.561 --> 00:00:07.582
achieves is a powerful diagnostic.

00:00:07.662 --> 00:00:14.502
It tells you whether the bottleneck is your
training method or a fundamental limit of the data and threat model.

00:00:14.582 --> 00:00:17.344
Past work delivered this only for two classes.

00:00:17.424 --> 00:00:22.163
Moving to many classes is not a trivial extension:
with three or more classes,

00:00:22.243 --> 00:00:27.477
examples can interact in higher-order ways that
binary analysis simply cannot capture,

00:00:27.557 --> 00:00:31.740
and these interactions can change what optimal
robustness looks like.
